ts the '{' is the next element to be processed. The right side depicts a st=
ack labeled 'stack' with its contents shown as '{' and '('; the label 'top:=
' indicates the top of the stack. A light-blue arrow labeled 'push { ' poin=
ts from the right to the stack, illustrating the 'push' operation where the=
 '{' character is being added to the top of the stack.  The overall diagram=
 demonstrates how a character ('{') is pushed onto a stack, which is a Last=
-In, First-Out (LIFO) data structure." loading=3D"lazy" width=3D"430" heigh=
t=3D"83" decoding=3D"async" data-nimg=3D"1" src=3D"https://bytebytego.com/i=
mages/courses/coding-patterns/stacks/valid-parenthesis-expression/image-07-=
01-7-2PAD6WHB.svg" style=3D"color: transparent;"></div></figure>
<hr>
<p>The next character is a closing parenthesis, =E2=80=98<code>)</code>=E2=
=80=99, which does not close the opening parenthesis at the top of the stac=
k, =E2=80=98<code>{</code>=E2=80=99. This means this parenthesis expression=
 is invalid. As such, we return false.</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: left;"=
><img alt=3D"Image represents a visual explanation of a stack-based approac=
